<!--
    A bike bearing a cog and a bolt: the same leg, in a city whose network
    lends both kinds side by side (SPEC §15).

    The bolt keeps the corner ic_bike_electric gave it and the cog sits under
    it, flush with the left edge, so that the two answer each other as one pair
    rather than facing off from opposite corners: what a motor helps to pedal,
    and what one pedals alone.

    The bike is drawn at nine tenths of its size, anchored to the bottom right.
    That is what the cog is worth: at full size the front wheel and the edge of
    the glyph leave it a radius of 2.30, which reads as a dot rather than as a
    cog; the tenth given up frees 2.85, and nothing is lost by it — a city
    lends one kind of fleet or the other, so the three drawings never appear
    side by side for the eye to compare their bikes.
-->
